        <p>FEVER HOSPITAL ARRA.VOEMENTS AT Sr. HELENS AND' A special meeting of th'e liaydock Local Board, pre- sided over by Mr. T. Grim ke Drayton, on Wednesday 3 'oint hospital arrangements Llavzocx. approved and confirmed the between that authority and th ',St. Helens Corporations whereby smallpox shall be trea led at Blackbrook and other cases of infectious disease ,at St. Helens. It was decided to adopt the Infectious Dist 'saes Notification Act for Haydock district. ti THE BATITING FATALITY."' Mr. Brighouse held an inquest at St. flellS function on Tuesday, on the body of John Robert AVson, aged 20, who was drowned in a pit of water ao:toining the Bold ironworks, in which be had gone to bathe' olf day afternoon. When he left home, at a qoarter to two, he did not say where he was going, and vitet4 his brother found his clothes on the side of the pit lOW an hour afterwards he suspected at once that his brothel', had been bathing and was drowned. The lifeless body w.s recovered by John Forber.—A verdict of "Accideut'- ally drowned whilst bathing "was returned.</p>
