        <head>SHOCKING DISCOVERY NEAR ST.</head>
        <p>SHOCKING DISCOVERY NEAR ST.</p>
        <p>HELENS,</p>
        <p>A CHILD'S BODY FOUND. IN A PIT OF WATER. James Ranson, a wheelwright, living at Windla Smithies, near St. Helens, was on fuesday night pass- ing a pit near Springfield, Eccleston, when he saw * bundle floating on the water. He pulled it out, and on removing the calico covering and opening a sheet of &amp; local newspaper he found the body of a child. The polio&amp; were sent for, and are now inquiring into the stair. Dr. Brooks, of Bainford, states that the body is that a a fully developed female child, and may have been in the wAter for a week.</p>
