      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-04-29_WidnesExaminer_art0085" n="art0085">
        <head>DRUNKENNESS AT 'WIDNES.</head>
        <p>DRUNKENNESS AT 'WIDNES.</p>
        <p>At Widnes Police Court on Monday the magistrates (the Mayor and Mr. Deacon) fined the:following persons for drunkenness —John Owen, Allorde-street ; William Hughes, West Bank-street • John Farley, St. Helens ; Michael Cain, Victoria-streA ; Frank Lachey, Moor-lane ; Francis Craven, Huyton ; Mary A. Smith, Wright-st. ; and George Wilkinson, Water-street. Both PRITCHARD'S Shops are under personal superrlalea.atil sustomera may rely upon raced Aug every attentlon.—Adet. GRNERAL DISTRICT RATE FOR RUNCORN. _ _ _ . .</p>
        <p>A special meeting of Runcorn Board of Cointnissioners was held at the Town Rail on Wednesday morning, under the presidency of Mr. F. Wiswall. Present Messrs. S. Taylor, W. Fisher, D. Bisbrown, R. Abel, F. A. Lake, (law clerk), and E. Marshall (secretary). On the motion of Mr. Fisher. seconded by Mr. Taylar, the seal of the Board was affixed to a general district rate of 2s. IOJ. in the for the year ending March 25th next. JOSEPH PRITCHARD, Watchmaker aad Jawallar, 61, Mfg-- it., and 4, Bridge-a,— Runc•ra.—Adet.</p>
