        <p>The Sanitary Wo-r-lx-s-6n-m-Q-tt-ee--b-a;e-rolved, on the recommendation of the Horses and Stables Sub-Commit- tee that the following horses be purchased :—A brown mare from Mr. Matthew Shakebhaft, of Lymm, for £BB ; and a brown horse from Mr. Enoch Sankey, of Croft, for £7l. •</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-04-29_WidnesExaminer_art0161" n="art0161">
        <head>OUTS TO THE MUSEUM.</head>
        <p>OUTS TO THE MUSEUM.</p>
        <p>The Museum Committee reports the following gifts := Fossils (8) from Ravenhead, St. Helens, from Councillor H. Roberts, J.P. ; coot shot at Halton, from Mr. James Jolley ; token issued by Thomas Hodgson, of Hington, in 1686, from Mr. N. Heywowt ; " British Flies," by Theo- bald, vol. 1., from Councillor Greening; plan of War. rington Parish Chnrch, 1821; map of Wargrive and Warrington Railtuay, kc.. from Mr. J. White, J.P. "The Synoptic Probleni,"bv A.J.Jolley from the author ;; "Catalogue of English Ballads ;*' "Vie de Carlos V. par Doublet," from Mr. Joseph Clare.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-04-29_WidnesExaminer_art0162" n="art0162">
        <head>TEE PICTURE GALLERY,</head>
        <p>TEE PICTURE GALLERY,</p>
        <p>The Museums. &amp;c., Committee have resolved that £l5O from du! Museum account be transferred to a' Picture Purchasing account " ; that the General Purposes Com- mittee be requested to transfer the Reamont Legacy Fund to the picture purchasing account; and that the Mayor he requested to approach Sir John Gilbert, R.A., with a vies'', of obtaining a gift from him for tho Art Gallery. The General Purposes Committee recommend in accordAnce with one of the above resolutions that the sum of £494 19s. Od., being the amount of the Beamont Legacy Fund, be trangerred to the" Picture Purchasing Account."</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-04-29_WidnesExaminer_art0163" n="art0163">
