      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-04-29_WidnesExaminer_art0164" n="art0164">
        <p>YnE DEMOUTIONB IN 4UNEU4.6T. The MEITLIL COMMittee Ve decided that the vacant ground in Queen-st be levelled arid cinderigd. THO frivieu now. AT uovrtair QUAY. The Rivers Committee have resolved that the borough surveyor be instructed to gauge the Sow of water in we river at Howley Quay,. and report thereon, frorn time to time ; and that be calf in a competent and verify the records made by him. person to 6UppOrt</p>
        <p>A NEW FIRE ENGINE:.-RECENT Mrs• .. The Fire Engine Committee nave resolved that an advertisement for anew Steam Eiigine„cuttahle of delivering 450 gallons per minute, be irimrted in ihe' "Engineer" and the" Ironmonger." The Superintend-1 ent has reported that fires hail occurred on thw farm premises of Mr: J. Lythgoe, Black Brook, Feaentiesci on the premises of the Highfieln Tanning Cotilirm'ff Runcorn ; and on premises belonging to Mr. Jos. WHO: - son, Longford-street. The Borough Treasurer has been instructed to forward the foliowing accounts for P 37- ment : Mr. J. Lythaoe, £l4 95. 611. ; the Highfield- Tanning Co., £2O 4s. 21. ; Mr. Jos. Wilkinson. t1.8a.6d. TIE WATER. COMMITTEE PROPOSED REMOVAL Or T36/F' OFFICES. The Water Committee has decided that the following' new mains be laid :-8-inch main from Wilson-Pattenst. to the baths ; 3-inch main in new street off Padttate- lane.;. and 3-inclr main in Bobsolt-st. It 'was reaolved that the Town Hall, Park, and Baths C9inmittee bo quested to make proviiod at the Town iall for the clerks and collectors of the Water Dopartment.</p>
        <p>A PeOFFISSIONAL AtIDITOIt WANTXD. The Goneral Purposes Committee recomMend tha.t the Town Clerk be instructed to advertise for applications for the appointment of a professional auditor at salary, o' £BO per annum. Candidates to be chartered accountants or members of the Incorporated 6ocietv of Accountants. , TUE SMALLPDX ITOSPPYAL.—A REQUEST TO nccedwiss. Councillor DIXON lias given notice of the illowitur motion :—"'That'the boarding across Dal:am-lane near the smallpox hospital be removod ; also that vlq Chair- man of the Health Committse be requested Ea reduce the cast of the hospital as much as possible."</p>
