        <p>The following tenders have been recommended for acceptance by the ditri-rent Committees t,--S•inittill Works Committee: Of the Warrington Slate Comp-int, Limited, to supply brown vitriol for twelve montbs, delivered free at Longford Works, at 35. pr ton; John Chorley, to supply six. dozen dustbins, at 5. 53' each ;.of Joseph Albinson' to. supply 1,000 oak caslcs• N. 10d. each; of Messrs. r: and J. Butteriiiiild and Co., Limited, to supply a lathe at £B5 175.„ and a drilling Machine at 260181., a:eject to the machines a,,,i tools being approved by the manager; of Henry Simon, of Manchester, to provide and erect an elevator and Con- veyors for refuse at Longford, Depot at £23s.—The 0116 COMMittell : Of Messrs. Chaphatu Brothers to supplY Cast iron tank at £137; according to specification ; 0' the Stanton Ironworks CO., to supply the followil cast iron pipes, 3-inch pipe at £4 4s. per ton ; inch pipe at £4 44. per ton; spetliatA, £7 175.. eto• per ton; of the Warrington State Co., Ltd., _„t° supply. 34,000 bricks at 2,8 a. per 1.000, delivered. Water Committee:: Of the Stanton Iron Works Cm,* Limited, to supply the east iron pipes required for the subway under the Manchester Ship Canal at TwettitY Steps Bridge at £822 13s. 51. ; of the Glenfield Compouni Limited, to supply the valves required for the ahoy° work at £164 es., 6.1.</p>
