      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-04-29_WidnesExaminer_art0166" n="art0166">
        <head>GYMNASIUM BAZAA It.</head>
        <p>THE GYMNASIUM BAZAA It.</p>
        <p>We should like to draw the attention of our readers to another bazaar at the Warrington Gy nasium. It will be opened on Wednesday next three o'clock by the Mayoress, Mrs. E. Greenaat and has for its object the assistance of what cau he claimed to be a public cause. IL is for the purpo'le of raising £7OO to wipe l'fl the building debt upou the Gymnasium, and as that institution has been erected for the benefit of all, tie stall-holders lie° week should not appeal to the generoSity of tile visitors in vain. Tie arranging of the building is being executed in a most atti active etyle more so than almost any beittar that Iles been held in the town, except perhaps the great Ice Carnival of two winters RP' The large room will be fitted out asap old English tov"' the designs are most pretty and the stalls and imitstinob of quaint old shops, will 'be under the charge of a laigs number if young ladies attired in picturesque costinne,!l: But the great feature is a moat uniros one. Benea.t".. the large room, is a large underground act° went which has been laid old and decorated ae grotto. It will accommodate quite ZOO persons, and be illuminated by electricity and tinted Japanese WO!. It is a most interesting place;, all rityls and corner_.-at and mysterious caverne,including one.place— where the is an enchanter. True, there will be many encitanters the upper floor, but this one is totally different irom others. The grotto is laid out in a manner wtich will effesi tively represent it as lined With glittering j „ ..wels '- r;reeinus atones. In ona part of itthere wid be a stiot:. ing gallery, and in another refreshtnent will be pefised. . Variety concerts will be. given. assisted the members of the Amateur Min-trels ; there diorama of the war in Egypt, and a Madam rougo,upes Exhibition. Ample details about prices, kc., iv, found in our advertising column .s. The Committee sy have had the arrangements of the affair in band are rro Messrs. T.Morris, Daniel .4nes.T. E. Wright and.). L'lrp. Whittle, Hugh Fergusson, Hesketh, D. Tinnion. d Welsh, J. Podmore, J., E. Warren, J. McGregor* it:10 others. The bazaar will be continued on Thuradai a Friday. will bed</p>
